Membership of j in GraphIdx of the enumerated set of maps coded by c is recursively enumerable jointly in the pair (c, j), relative to any valid function-space presentation. Unfolded, the membership is an existential quantification over two witnesses n and m₀ of a primitive-recursive check, an inclusion of enumerated sets, and a bit test.

The function-space presentation supplies a recursively decidable inclusion of enumerated sets of maps. Packing a state as m₀, then n, then c, then j, the following are recursively decidable: equality of the untagged list of j with bitsCode n n, inclusion of the enumerated set coded by c in the enumerated singleton step of n and m₀, and the assertion that the bit of m₀ at the untagged value of j is set. The first is a primitive-recursive equality, the second is the presentation inclusion along a primitive-recursive reindexing, and the third is bitAt. Their conjunction is recursively enumerable. Projecting away m₀ and then n leaves a predicate of the pair. Rewriting by the decoded membership criterion for GraphIdx, a witness produces the packed checks, with the universal relation rewritten as the singleton-step inclusion, and a packed witness unpacks to the same data in the other direction.
